",\n   188→    \"date\": \"2026-08-09\",\n   189→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   190→  },\n   191→  {\n   192→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   193→    \"title\": \"v0.147.0 - Agent Plugins and conversation organization\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"Install portable Agent Plugins and search across local, personal, workspace, and remote plugin catalogs. Organize conversations into persistent, manually ordered sections. New --approve-for-me flag for automatically reviewed approvals. Import from Cursor-managed skills. Support for opt-in MCP 2026-07-28 protocol with paginated discovery.\",\n   195→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   196→    \"url\": \"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\",\n   197→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   198→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   199→  },\n   200→  {\n   201→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   202→    \"title\": \"Daybreak Blue and Daybreak Red security tiers\",\n   203→    \"description\": \"Two access tiers for approved defenders in security work. Daybreak Blue for defensive security work with GPT-5.6 Sol model. Daybreak Red for authorized vulnerability reproduction and red teaming with GPT-5.6 Cyber model. Both require approval through Trusted Access for Cyber.\",\n   204→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   205→    \"url\": \"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\",\n   206→    \"date\": \"2026-08-10\",\n   207→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   208→  },\n   209→  {\n   210→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   211→    \"title\": \"Agent Import functionality and Linux Desktop Preview\",\n   212→    \"description\": \"Support for importing from Claude Code, Claude Cowork, and Cursor including instructions, settings, skills, plugins, projects, and recent work. ChatGPT desktop app for Linux available for Ubuntu, Debian, and Fedora on x64 and ARM64 processors.\",\n   213→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   214→    \"url\": \"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\",\n   215→    \"date\": \"2026-08-11\",\n   216→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   217→  },\n   218→  {\n   219→    \"productName\": \"Codex CLI\",\n   220→    \"title\": \"Computer History for macOS\",\n   221→    \"description\": \"Feature in macOS desktop app that converts activity across applications and websites into memories and timeline that ChatGPT and Codex can use. Users can control which apps and websites contribute, pause collection, and review or delete history. Limited to Pro, Business, and Enterprise users.\",\n   222→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   223→    \"url\": \"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\",\n   224→    \"date\": \"2026-08-13\",\n   225→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   226→  },\n   227→  {\n   228→    \"productName\": \"Gemini CLI\",\n   229→    \"title\": \"v0.54.0 - PR Automation and security enhancements\",\n   230→    \"description\": \"Integrated Antigravity agent runner with dual-locking Firestore concurrency controls for PR generator. Enhanced caretaker triage to post comments prior to auto-closing issues. Prevented cleartext credential leakage by enforcing HTTPS, rotated session IDs on model fallbacks, and skipped merged function-response turns.\",\n   231→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   232→    \"url\": \"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\",\n   233→    \"date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   234→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   235→  }\n   236→]\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
